{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f5371174-bba0-4992-a14b-d71ea13c02eb","agentId":"ac3048c66f3643aa6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (live layer cuore/live/: capture.py, learn.py, learned.py, did_catalog.py, uds.py, stream.py; mes recordings parser in mes-log-mcp/mes/csvlog*.py). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, never open COM3; fakes only; ≤6 suites. Another agent owns system_detail_bridge/system.html/_transmission.html/m_home/owner_routes: do not edit. You own NEW cuore/live/mes_learn.py, cuore/api/mes_learn.py (+ app.py include pair), NEW templates/mes_learn.html + cuore/web/mes_learn_routes.py (+ include pair), one marked tool block in obd2-mcp/server.py, cuore/live/learned.py (additive), docs/handbook/07-first-live-session.md (additive section), cuore/tests/check_mes_learn.py. You may commit and push (`github` main only; never koch-mcp/). Report under 120 words.\n\nBuild the software side of \"learn module parameters from MES\": with a Y-splitter on the OBD port, a SECOND adapter (another STN/vLinker on its own COM port, or a USB-CAN interface) listens passively on CAN-C (pins 6/14; through the gateway it carries MES's UDS requests and the modules' responses) while MES runs its live view and records a CSV. CUORE captures every request/response pair (ISO-TP reassembled; 29-bit 18DAxxF1/18DAF1xx and 11-bit pairs), groups by module and DID (service 0x22 request → 0x62 response, 0x21 local ids, 0x2A periodic), timestamps them, then aligns the raw response byte series against the MES CSV recording's named parameter columns by time: for each named column, find the (module, DID, byte offset, width, signedness) and the linear scale/offset that best fit (least squares over the session; require ≥0.98 R² and ≥20 distinct values, else \"no confident match\"). Output: learned DID definitions saved via cuore/live/learned.py with source \"learned from MES <csv name> <date>, fit R² x\", confidence \"SINGLE-SOURCE (learned)\", never overwriting catalogue DIDs; a review page /v/{vin}/learn-mes listing candidates with the fit plot numbers and Accept/Reject (accept = usable by the Live board as a named, scaled channel; reject = kept as unscaled). Guards: the second adapter must be a different port than MES's (interlock.mes_status gives MES's port); the listener never transmits (STCMM 0 / monitor only); refuse if only one adapter is present with a clear message naming what is needed (Y-splitter + second adapter). API: POST /api/mes-learn/start {port}, /stop, GET /status, GET /candidates, POST /candidates/{id}/accept|reject. MCP tools in the marked block: mes_learn_start/stop/status/candidates/accept. Tests with a synthetic capture (two modules, three DIDs, one 2-byte signed temperature scaled 0.1 with offset -40, one 1-byte gear) and a synthetic MES CSV: candidates found with the right offset/scale, R² reported, accept makes a Live board channel (via channels/learned), single-adapter refusal, never transmits (fake stream asserts no non-AT/ST command sent). Handbook: \"Learning module parameters from MES\" with the hardware list. Commit \"Learn module DIDs by listening to MES over a second adapter: capture, align to the MES recording, review and accept\" with the Co-Authored-By line, push, report hash."},"uuid":"cf7806a5-3a26-4cf4-bf39-23368e021913","timestamp":"2026-10-14T17:56:53.189Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
