{"parentUuid":"0114a9a5-a0db-4afb-876d-f96a2ff44133","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"2fb62f54-c7c9-43d1-b80f-515baf3fab1f","agentId":"ac3048c66f3643aa6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UPnSSznPhtN8Moz3hxMcrJ","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (310.6KB). Full output saved to: C:\\Users\\User\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\tool-results\\btg4h2yf8.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\ncuore/live/buses.py:115:        \"set STCMM 0 before STPO when the rate is in doubt.\"\ncuore/live/buses.py:140:        \"with STCMM 0 + STM. FEPS hazard: the vLinker FS is a Ford tool \"\ncuore/live/capture.py:5:byte itself. Sessions are opened ``passive=True``, which sets ``STCMM 0``\ncuore/live/did_catalog.py:301:# targets and carry no request/response pair; a passive listen (STCMM 0)\ncuore/live/transport.py:585:            # STCMM persists across port closes; a passive listen must not\ncuore/live/transport.py:587:            sess.cmd(\"STCMM 0\" if sess.passive else \"STCMM 1\", 2)\ncuore/tests/check_active_probe.py:113:    \"STCMM 0\": \"OK\", \"STCMM 1\": \"OK\",\ncuore/tests/check_coverage.py:347:check(\"a request session puts the adapter in normal CAN mode\", \"STCMM 1\" in bus.sent,\ncuore/tests/check_dtc_detail.py:236:    \"STP 34\": \"OK\", \"STCMM 1\": \"OK\",\ncuore/tests/check_live.py:261:    (\"STCMM 0\", \"adapter_state\"), (\"STFPA 7E8,7FF\", \"adapter_state\"),\ncuore/tests/check_live.py:538:    \"STCMM 0\": \"OK\",\ncuore/tests/check_transport_perf.py:78:    \"STCMM 0\": \"OK\", \"STCMM 1\": \"OK\",\nobd2-mcp/server.py:646:        # and must not run under STCMM 0 (receive-only, no ACK).\nobd2-mcp/tests/test_fixes.py:130:    (\"STCMM 0\", \"adapter_state\"), (\"STFPA 7E8,7FF\", \"adapter_state\"),\ndocs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:32:| `STCMM 0` makes the adapter receive without acknowledging. | Passive capture is possible with the Security Gateway locked and is the safest operation in the design. |\ndocs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:53:    capture.py       passive monitor: STCMM 0 + filters + STM, frame store, DBC decode\ndocs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:79:2. **Verify before transmit.** The first session on a newly declared bus is passive: `STCMM 0`, open, `STMA 50`. If frames arrive at the expected rate, the bus is marked `verified` for this cable state. If not, the bus stays `unverified` and transmit is refused with a message naming the cable to check.\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"44f7d888-18f5-4866-855f-424a248889f6","timestamp":"2026-10-14T18:00:39.342Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"cuore/live/buses.py:115:        \"set STCMM 0 before STPO when the rate is in doubt.\"\ncuore/live/buses.py:140:        \"with STCMM 0 + STM. FEPS hazard: the vLinker FS is a Ford tool \"\ncuore/live/capture.py:5:byte itself. Sessions are opened ``passive=True``, which sets ``STCMM 0``\ncuore/live/did_catalog.py:301:# targets and carry no request/response pair; a passive listen (STCMM 0)\ncuore/live/transport.py:585:            # STCMM persists across port closes; a passive listen must not\ncuore/live/transport.py:587:            sess.cmd(\"STCMM 0\" if sess.passive else \"STCMM 1\", 2)\ncuore/tests/check_active_probe.py:113:    \"STCMM 0\": \"OK\", \"STCMM 1\": \"OK\",\ncuore/tests/check_coverage.py:347:check(\"a request session puts the adapter in normal CAN mode\", \"STCMM 1\" in bus.sent,\ncuore/tests/check_dtc_detail.py:236:    \"STP 34\": \"OK\", \"STCMM 1\": \"OK\",\ncuore/tests/check_live.py:261:    (\"STCMM 0\", \"adapter_state\"), (\"STFPA 7E8,7FF\", \"adapter_state\"),\ncuore/tests/check_live.py:538:    \"STCMM 0\": \"OK\",\ncuore/tests/check_transport_perf.py:78:    \"STCMM 0\": \"OK\", \"STCMM 1\": \"OK\",\nobd2-mcp/server.py:646:        # and must not run under STCMM 0 (receive-only, no ACK).\nobd2-mcp/tests/test_fixes.py:130:    (\"STCMM 0\", \"adapter_state\"), (\"STFPA 7E8,7FF\", \"adapter_state\"),\ndocs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:32:| `STCMM 0` makes the adapter receive without acknowledging. | Passive capture is possible with the Security Gateway locked and is the safest operation in the design. |\ndocs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:53:    capture.py       passive monitor: STCMM 0 + filters + STM, frame store, DBC decode\ndocs/design/CUORE_LIVE_LINK_PLAN.md:79:2. **Verify before transmit.** The first session on a newly declared bus is passive: `STCMM 0`, open, `STMA 50`. If frames arrive at the expected rate, the bus is marked `verified` for this cable state. If not, the bus stays `unverified` and transmit is refused with a message naming the cable to check.\ndocs/design/review-2026-09-14/cuore_survey.md:302:  no `STCMM`, no `STFPA`, no `STBR`. Confirmed by grep across the whole package: zero hits for\ndocs/design/review-2026-09-14/cuore_survey.md:667:    capture.py         # passive monitor: STCMM 0 + STM/STMA, frame store\ndocs/design/review-2026-09-14/cuore_survey.md:790:# STCMM 0 (listen-only, no ACK) -> STFPA pass filters -> STM/STMA -> read until deadline\ndocs/design/review-2026-09-14/cuore_survey.md:854:  B2 (`STP 54` for CAN-IHS on pins 3/11), B3 (passive capture: `STCMM 0` + `STM`/`STMA` + `STFPA`),\ndocs/handbook/02-architecture.md:119:- **Bus capture**: `POST /api/live/capture` (`cuore/live/capture.py`) listens passively (`STCMM 0`, no CAN ACK) and returns the raw frame list; it does **not** persist an observation today -- the frames go back to the caller only.\ndocs/handbook/07-first-live-session.md:321:below is read-only (passive listen, `STCMM 0` + `STM`/`ATMA`) -- the\ndocs/reference/GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md:101:| CAN-IHS (body / comfort / infotainment) | 3 (+) / 11 (−) | DB D434 / WH D433 | 125 kbps `CONFIRMED` | 29-bit presumed | blue A5 (6→3, 14→11), or possibly none | With A5: `STP 34` then `STPBR 125000`. Without A5: `STP 54` (MS-CAN transceiver on adapter pins 3/11) `UNVERIFIED` | HVAC, ETM, AMP, ESEM, CSWM, CRSM, LBSS, RBSS, PLGM (all `UNVERIFIED` on this car) | Do not mix routes: with the A5 fitted, adapter pins 3/11 map to nothing defined, so use the HS preset plus `STPBR`, never `STP 53/54`. Opening a 500 k preset on a 125 k bus emits error frames; set `STCMM 0` before `STPO` when the rate is in doubt. |\ndocs/reference/GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md:102:| CAN-CH (chassis / ADAS / safety) | 12 (+) / 13 (−) | GN/WH D478 / BN/WH D477 | 500 kbps `INFERRED` (never measured) | 29-bit presumed | grey A6 (6→12, 14→13), mandatory: the STN1170 has no transceiver on pins 12/13 | `STP 34`; if silent, `STP 36` (250 k) then `STPBR 125000` | ABS/ESC, EPS, ORC, AFLS, PAM, HALF (TVM, ESL not answering) | Never transmit on CAN-CH without explicit human confirmation: brakes, airbag squibs and steering assist live here. Listen first with `STCMM 0` + `STM`. FEPS hazard: the vLinker FS is a Ford tool whose 18 V FEPS output is OBD pin 13, which on Giorgio is CAN-CH(−). Never issue any FEPS or programming-voltage command on this vehicle; whether the FS can be commanded to FEPS over serial is `UNVERIFIED`, treat as live. |\ndocs/reference/GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md:179:STCMM 0          # receive only, no CAN ACK\ndocs/reference/GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md:199:STCMM 0\ndocs/reference/GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md:233:Sweep CAN-C first; sweep CAN-CH only after Q3 and with `STCMM 0` proven.\ndocs/reference/STELVIO_READABLE_ITEMS.md:222:means a passive listen (`STCMM 0`) on whichever bus carries them, which this\ndocs/research/MES_DEEP_INTEGRATION_REVIEW.md:121:**A5. Fix the OBD server before extending it.** Baud from registry (115200), `ATH1`, pin the protocol after detection, JSON returns, `adapter_error()` on every tool, reject embedded CR/LF in `send_raw`, classify `ST` commands (allowlist reads such as `STI`, `STDI`, `STPRS`, `STSLCS`; gate `STPX`, `STP`, `STBR`, `STWBR`, `STCMM`), and make `clear_dtcs` capture DTCs plus freeze frames plus readiness before clearing and read back after.\ndocs/research/MES_DEEP_INTEGRATION_REVIEW.md:135:**B3. Passive CAN capture.** `STCMM 0` (receive only, no ACK) plus `STM` or `STMA` with `STFPA` pass filters and `STBR` raised toward 2 Mbps. The adapter never transmits, so it works with the Security Gateway fully locked and is the safest item in this document. Feed frames through `cantools` with the opendbc Giorgio DBC (PR 1251) or the repo's own `fca_giorgio.dbc` notes; `0x0F1` is the 100 Hz voltage signal the platform research ranks as the single most valuable measurement. Budget for `OUT OF MEMORY` from filter allocation.\ndocs/research/MES_DEEP_INTEGRATION_REVIEW.md:148:- **C4. Second adapter on a Y-splitter** so MES and Claude can co-exist. Electrically fine on CAN; keep the Claude side in `STCMM 0` so only one node ACKs.\ndocs/research/MES_DEEP_INTEGRATION_REVIEW.md:179:2. `STP 54`, `STPBRR`, `STPO`, `STCMM 0`, `STM 50` to see whether CAN-IHS traffic appears on pins 3/11 without the blue cable.\ndocs/research/OBD_CONNECTIVITY_REVIEW_2026-10-14.md:20:`STP <protocol>`/`STPBR`/`STCMM`), yields a `Session`, and closes the port on the way out —\ndocs/research/review-2026-09-14/web_research.md:156:- **`STCMM mode`** — CAN monitoring mode, and this one matters for safety:\ndocs/research/review-2026-09-14/web_research.md:205:**Periodic Messaging (§8.14, p.50)** — `STPPMA` adds background auto-sent messages. **This is your TesterPresent (`3E 00`) keepalive** for extended diagnostic sessions, handled by the adapter rather than your event loop. Caveats: protocol must be open; `STCMM` mode governs whether periodic messages are sent while monitoring; `OUT OF MEMORY` risk as with filters; you must account for periodic-message replies when parsing responses to manual requests.\ndocs/research/review-2026-09-14/web_research.md:357:**Difficulty:** Low. **Risk:** Low — start with `STCMM 0` (no ACK) + `STM` to listen before transmitting. **Verify before building on it.**\ndocs/research/review-2026-09-14/web_research.md:359:### 3. Passive raw-CAN sniffer/recorder (`STCMM 0` + `STM`/`STMA` + `STFPA`)\ndocs/research/review-2026-09-14/web_research.md:362:**Difficulty:** Low–Medium. **Risk:** Very low with `STCMM 0` — the adapter does not even ACK. **The safest thing in this list.**\ndocs/research/review-2026-09-14/web_research.md:376:**Prereqs:** process watch + `SerialPort` open/close discipline; optionally a second adapter on a second COM port (the car OBD port is single, so this means a Y-splitter — electrically fine on CAN, but two ACKing nodes; set the passive one to `STCMM 0`).\ndocs/research/WITECH_PASSIVE_LEARNING.md:92:  `passive=True`, which sets `STCMM 0` on the STN adapter — no CAN\ndocs/research/WITECH_PASSIVE_LEARNING.md:103:- **Confirm STCMM 0 before trusting the capture as passive.** `capture.py`\ndocs/sessions/raw/2026-10-13/7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17/tasks/a064032b3180b0755.output:16:{\"parentUuid\":\"3527319a-abde-42c2-b4f5-2345fabe80f4\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"f74369e0-f2ed-48b3-a759-5aa42e975543\",\"agentId\":\"a064032b3180b0755\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01T8XJJ6V3zkU1NoYFsn7jR4\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"---buses.py---\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Pure-data description of the Giorgio-platform CAN buses on this car.\\n\\nSource of truth: docs/reference/GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md (Table B, the\\nstructural finding, and the hazard entries). This module encodes exactly\\nwhat that document says. Where the document says \\\"unknown\\\", this module\\nuses ``None``. Confidences are never upgraded past what the document\\nstates.\\n\\nStdlib only.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\n\\nCABLES = (\\\"none\\\", \\\"blue_a5\\\", \\\"grey_a6\\\")\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass Route:\\n    cable: str  # one of CABLES\\n    stn_protocol: str  # STN \\\"STP\\\" preset number as a string, e.g. \\\"34\\\", \\\"54\\\"\\n    bitrate_override: int | None  # e.g. 125000 when the HS preset must be re-rated after a re-pinning cable\\n    status: str  # \\\"confirmed\\\" | \\\"untested\\\" | \\\"unreachable\\\"\\n    note: str\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass Bus:\\n    key: str  # \\\"can_c\\\" | \\\"can_ihs\\\" | \\\"can_ch\\\"\\n    name: str\\n    pins: tuple[int, int]\\n    bitrate: int  # the bus's own bitrate\\n    bitrate_confidence: str  # \\\"confirmed\\\" | \\\"inferred\\\"\\n    id_bits: int  # 29\\n    routes: tuple[Route, ...]  # every way to reach it, in preference order\\n    transmit_needs_confirmation: bool  # True for can_ch\\n    modules_seen: tuple[str, ...]  # MES codes actually observed on this bus on this car\\n    notes: str  # safety text from Table B\\n\\n\\nCAN_C = Bus(\\n    key=\\\"can_c\\\",\\n    name=\\\"CAN-C (diagnostic / powertrain)\\\",\\n    pins=(6, 14),\\n    bitrate=500000,\\n    bitrate_confidence=\\\"confirmed\\\",\\n    id_bits=29,\\n    routes=(\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"none\\\",\\n            \\\"34\\\",\\n            None,\\n            \\\"confirmed\\\",\\n            \\\"STP 34 (or STP 33 for the legislated 11-bit 7E0/7E8 pair); STPBRR expected 500000. \\\"\\n            \\\"On 2018+ Giorgio cars (Security Gateway Module) CAN-C is gateway-isolated: there is \\\"\\n            \\\"NO broadcast traffic on it at all, in either width -- a passive listen on STP 34 \\\"\\n            \\\"reading 0 frames does not mean the bus is dead. See the STP 33 route's note; \\\"\\n            \\\"ops.verify_bus() falls back to an active Mode 01 PID 00 probe for exactly this case.\\\",\\n        ),\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"none\\\",\\n            \\\"33\\\",\\n            None,\\n            \\\"untested\\\",\\n            \\\"11-bit legislated pair 7E0/7E8 at 500k. Giorgio broadcast traffic on CAN-C is \\\"\\n            \\\"largely 11-bit, so a monitor opened 29-bit-only can report zero frames on a \\\"\\n            \\\"perfectly healthy bus. Listened for after STP 34, never preferred for UDS. On \\\"\\n            \\\"2018+ cars behind the Security Gateway Module this route still carries no \\\"\\n            \\\"broadcast traffic either -- the gateway only answers a request, it never emits \\\"\\n            \\\"anything unprompted -- so a passive listen here is also 0 frames on a healthy \\\"\\n            \\\"car; verification instead sends one legislated Mode 01 PID 00 request (7DF) and \\\"\\n            \\\"accepts any 7E8-7EF reply as proof the bus is alive.\\\",\\n        ),\\n    ),\\n    transmit_needs_confirmation=False,\\n    modules_seen=(\\\"ECM\\\", \\\"IPC\\\", \\\"TCM\\\", \\\"DTCM\\\", \\\"ESM\\\", \\\"BCM\\\", \\\"RFHUB\\\", \\\"DASM\\\"),\\n    notes=(\\n        \\\"Live powertrain bus. Writes gated. Whole-vehicle serial UDS sweeps \\\"\\n        \\\"manufacture -87/-2F bystander codes (SCAN_2609041953 shows exactly \\\"\\n        \\\"that: DTCM U0100-87, BCM U171x-2F, EPS U1960-83). Pull DTC EX before \\\"\\n        \\\"clearing.\\\"\\n    ),\\n)\\n\\nCAN_IHS = Bus(\\n    key=\\\"can_ihs\\\",\\n    name=\\\"CAN-IHS (body / comfort / infotainment)\\\",\\n    pins=(3, 11),\\n    bitrate=125000,\\n    bitrate_confidence=\\\"confirmed\\\",\\n    id_bits=29,\\n    routes=(\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"blue_a5\\\",\\n            \\\"34\\\",\\n            125000,\\n            \\\"untested\\\",\\n            \\\"HS transceiver re-pinned onto 3/11 by the cable; never use STP 53/54 with the cable fitted\\\",\\n        ),\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"none\\\",\\n            \\\"54\\\",\\n            None,\\n            \\\"untested\\\",\\n            \\\"MS-CAN transceiver on adapter pins 3/11; verify STPRS changes and STPBRR reads 125000; auto-switch firmware may override\\\",\\n        ),\\n    ),\\n    transmit_needs_confirmation=False,\\n    modules_seen=(),\\n    notes=(\\n        \\\"Do not mix routes: with the A5 fitted, adapter pins 3/11 map to \\\"\\n        \\\"nothing defined, so use the HS preset plus STPBR, never STP \\\"\\n        \\\"53/54. Opening a 500k preset on a 125k bus emits error frames; \\\"\\n        \\\"set STCMM 0 before STPO when the rate is in doubt.\\\"\\n    ),\\n)\\n\\nCAN_CH = Bus(\\n    key=\\\"can_ch\\\",\\n    name=\\\"CAN-CH (chassis / ADAS / safety)\\\",\\n    pins=(12, 13),\\n    bitrate=500000,\\n    bitrate_confidence=\\\"inferred\\\",\\n    id_bits=29,\\n    routes=(\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"grey_a6\\\",\\n            \\\"34\\\",\\n            None,\\n            \\\"confirmed\\\",\\n            \\\"bitrate inferred 500k; if silent try STP 36 then STPBR 125000\\\",\\n        ),\\n    ),\\n    transmit_needs_confirmation=True,\\n    modules_seen=(\\\"ABS\\\", \\\"EPS\\\", \\\"ORC\\\", \\\"AFLS\\\", \\\"PAM\\\", \\\"HALF\\\"),\\n    notes=(\\n        \\\"Never transmit on CAN-CH without explicit human confirmation: \\\"\\n        \\\"brakes, airbag squibs and steering assist live here. Listen first \\\"\\n        \\\"with STCMM 0 + STM. FEPS hazard: the vLinker FS is a Ford tool \\\"\\n        \\\"whose 18V FEPS output is OBD pin 13, which on Giorgio is \\\"\\n        \\\"CAN-CH(-). Never issue any FEPS or programming-voltage command on \\\"\\n        \\\"this vehicle; whether the FS can be commanded to FEPS over serial \\\"\\n        \\\"is UNVERIFIED, treat as live.\\\"\\n    ),\\n)\\n\\nBUSES: dict[str, Bus] = {\\n    \\\"can_c\\\": CAN_C,\\n    \\\"can_ihs\\\": CAN_IHS,\\n    \\\"can_ch\\\": CAN_CH,\\n}\\n\\nPIN_1_9_WARNING = (\\n    \\\"do not use modified interfaces with a short between pins 1 and 9 on \\\"\\n    \\\"Giulia or Stelvio; it drops the bus. Continuity-check any cable \\\"\\n    \\\"before fitting.\\\"\\n)\\n\\n_HEADER_BITS_BY_PROTOCOL: dict[str, int] = {\\n    # ISO 15765-4 CAN STN \\\"STP\\\" preset numbers.\\n    \\\"31\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"33\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"35\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"51\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"53\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"32\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"34\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"36\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"52\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"54\\\": 29,\\n    # ELM-style short forms.\\n    \\\"6\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"8\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"7\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"9\\\": 29,\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef route_for(bus: Bus, cable: str) -> Route | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The route on ``bus`` that works with ``cable``, or None.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    for route in bus.routes:\\n        if route.cable == cable:\\n            return route\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef routes_for(bus: Bus, cable: str) -> list[Route]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every route on ``bus`` that works with ``cable``, in preference order.\\n\\n    A bus can be reachable under more than one adapter protocol. ``route_for``\\n    returns the preferred one and is what normal operations use; this returns\\n    the full candidate list, so a passive listen can try them all before\\n    concluding a bus is silent.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return [route for route in bus.routes if route.cable == cable]\\n\\n\\ndef buses_for_cable(cable: str) -> list[Bus]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Buses reachable with ``cable``, in preference order.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    result = []\\n    for bus in BUSES.values():\\n        if route_for(bus, cable) is not None:\\n            result.append(bus)\\n    return result\\n\\n\\ndef header_bits_for_protocol(stn_protocol: str) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"11 or 29, per the STN STP preset (or ELM short form).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return _HEADER_BITS_BY_PROTOCOL[stn_protocol]\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"uuid\":\"115d184d-2ebf-4b02-882b-0ab361039d05\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-14T05:28:45.319Z\",\"toolUseResult\":{\"stdout\":\"---buses.py---\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Pure-data description of the Giorgio-platform CAN buses on this car.\\n\\nSource of truth: docs/reference/GIORGIO_MODULE_MAP.md (Table B, the\\nstructural finding, and the hazard entries). This module encodes exactly\\nwhat that document says. Where the document says \\\"unknown\\\", this module\\nuses ``None``. Confidences are never upgraded past what the document\\nstates.\\n\\nStdlib only.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\n\\nCABLES = (\\\"none\\\", \\\"blue_a5\\\", \\\"grey_a6\\\")\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass Route:\\n    cable: str  # one of CABLES\\n    stn_protocol: str  # STN \\\"STP\\\" preset number as a string, e.g. \\\"34\\\", \\\"54\\\"\\n    bitrate_override: int | None  # e.g. 125000 when the HS preset must be re-rated after a re-pinning cable\\n    status: str  # \\\"confirmed\\\" | \\\"untested\\\" | \\\"unreachable\\\"\\n    note: str\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass Bus:\\n    key: str  # \\\"can_c\\\" | \\\"can_ihs\\\" | \\\"can_ch\\\"\\n    name: str\\n    pins: tuple[int, int]\\n    bitrate: int  # the bus's own bitrate\\n    bitrate_confidence: str  # \\\"confirmed\\\" | \\\"inferred\\\"\\n    id_bits: int  # 29\\n    routes: tuple[Route, ...]  # every way to reach it, in preference order\\n    transmit_needs_confirmation: bool  # True for can_ch\\n    modules_seen: tuple[str, ...]  # MES codes actually observed on this bus on this car\\n    notes: str  # safety text from Table B\\n\\n\\nCAN_C = Bus(\\n    key=\\\"can_c\\\",\\n    name=\\\"CAN-C (diagnostic / powertrain)\\\",\\n    pins=(6, 14),\\n    bitrate=500000,\\n    bitrate_confidence=\\\"confirmed\\\",\\n    id_bits=29,\\n    routes=(\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"none\\\",\\n            \\\"34\\\",\\n            None,\\n            \\\"confirmed\\\",\\n            \\\"STP 34 (or STP 33 for the legislated 11-bit 7E0/7E8 pair); STPBRR expected 500000. \\\"\\n            \\\"On 2018+ Giorgio cars (Security Gateway Module) CAN-C is gateway-isolated: there is \\\"\\n            \\\"NO broadcast traffic on it at all, in either width -- a passive listen on STP 34 \\\"\\n            \\\"reading 0 frames does not mean the bus is dead. See the STP 33 route's note; \\\"\\n            \\\"ops.verify_bus() falls back to an active Mode 01 PID 00 probe for exactly this case.\\\",\\n        ),\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"none\\\",\\n            \\\"33\\\",\\n            None,\\n            \\\"untested\\\",\\n            \\\"11-bit legislated pair 7E0/7E8 at 500k. Giorgio broadcast traffic on CAN-C is \\\"\\n            \\\"largely 11-bit, so a monitor opened 29-bit-only can report zero frames on a \\\"\\n            \\\"perfectly healthy bus. Listened for after STP 34, never preferred for UDS. On \\\"\\n            \\\"2018+ cars behind the Security Gateway Module this route still carries no \\\"\\n            \\\"broadcast traffic either -- the gateway only answers a request, it never emits \\\"\\n            \\\"anything unprompted -- so a passive listen here is also 0 frames on a healthy \\\"\\n            \\\"car; verification instead sends one legislated Mode 01 PID 00 request (7DF) and \\\"\\n            \\\"accepts any 7E8-7EF reply as proof the bus is alive.\\\",\\n        ),\\n    ),\\n    transmit_needs_confirmation=False,\\n    modules_seen=(\\\"ECM\\\", \\\"IPC\\\", \\\"TCM\\\", \\\"DTCM\\\", \\\"ESM\\\", \\\"BCM\\\", \\\"RFHUB\\\", \\\"DASM\\\"),\\n    notes=(\\n        \\\"Live powertrain bus. Writes gated. Whole-vehicle serial UDS sweeps \\\"\\n        \\\"manufacture -87/-2F bystander codes (SCAN_2609041953 shows exactly \\\"\\n        \\\"that: DTCM U0100-87, BCM U171x-2F, EPS U1960-83). Pull DTC EX before \\\"\\n        \\\"clearing.\\\"\\n    ),\\n)\\n\\nCAN_IHS = Bus(\\n    key=\\\"can_ihs\\\",\\n    name=\\\"CAN-IHS (body / comfort / infotainment)\\\",\\n    pins=(3, 11),\\n    bitrate=125000,\\n    bitrate_confidence=\\\"confirmed\\\",\\n    id_bits=29,\\n    routes=(\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"blue_a5\\\",\\n            \\\"34\\\",\\n            125000,\\n            \\\"untested\\\",\\n            \\\"HS transceiver re-pinned onto 3/11 by the cable; never use STP 53/54 with the cable fitted\\\",\\n        ),\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"none\\\",\\n            \\\"54\\\",\\n            None,\\n            \\\"untested\\\",\\n            \\\"MS-CAN transceiver on adapter pins 3/11; verify STPRS changes and STPBRR reads 125000; auto-switch firmware may override\\\",\\n        ),\\n    ),\\n    transmit_needs_confirmation=False,\\n    modules_seen=(),\\n    notes=(\\n        \\\"Do not mix routes: with the A5 fitted, adapter pins 3/11 map to \\\"\\n        \\\"nothing defined, so use the HS preset plus STPBR, never STP \\\"\\n        \\\"53/54. Opening a 500k preset on a 125k bus emits error frames; \\\"\\n        \\\"set STCMM 0 before STPO when the rate is in doubt.\\\"\\n    ),\\n)\\n\\nCAN_CH = Bus(\\n    key=\\\"can_ch\\\",\\n    name=\\\"CAN-CH (chassis / ADAS / safety)\\\",\\n    pins=(12, 13),\\n    bitrate=500000,\\n    bitrate_confidence=\\\"inferred\\\",\\n    id_bits=29,\\n    routes=(\\n        Route(\\n            \\\"grey_a6\\\",\\n            \\\"34\\\",\\n            None,\\n            \\\"confirmed\\\",\\n            \\\"bitrate inferred 500k; if silent try STP 36 then STPBR 125000\\\",\\n        ),\\n    ),\\n    transmit_needs_confirmation=True,\\n    modules_seen=(\\\"ABS\\\", \\\"EPS\\\", \\\"ORC\\\", \\\"AFLS\\\", \\\"PAM\\\", \\\"HALF\\\"),\\n    notes=(\\n        \\\"Never transmit on CAN-CH without explicit human confirmation: \\\"\\n        \\\"brakes, airbag squibs and steering assist live here. Listen first \\\"\\n        \\\"with STCMM 0 + STM. FEPS hazard: the vLinker FS is a Ford tool \\\"\\n        \\\"whose 18V FEPS output is OBD pin 13, which on Giorgio is \\\"\\n        \\\"CAN-CH(-). Never issue any FEPS or programming-voltage command on \\\"\\n        \\\"this vehicle; whether the FS can be commanded to FEPS over serial \\\"\\n        \\\"is UNVERIFIED, treat as live.\\\"\\n    ),\\n)\\n\\nBUSES: dict[str, Bus] = {\\n    \\\"can_c\\\": CAN_C,\\n    \\\"can_ihs\\\": CAN_IHS,\\n    \\\"can_ch\\\": CAN_CH,\\n}\\n\\nPIN_1_9_WARNING = (\\n    \\\"do not use modified interfaces with a short between pins 1 and 9 on \\\"\\n    \\\"Giulia or Stelvio; it drops the bus. Continuity-check any cable \\\"\\n    \\\"before fitting.\\\"\\n)\\n\\n_HEADER_BITS_BY_PROTOCOL: dict[str, int] = {\\n    # ISO 15765-4 CAN STN \\\"STP\\\" preset numbers.\\n    \\\"31\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"33\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"35\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"51\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"53\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"32\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"34\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"36\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"52\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"54\\\": 29,\\n    # ELM-style short forms.\\n    \\\"6\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"8\\\": 11,\\n    \\\"7\\\": 29,\\n    \\\"9\\\": 29,\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef route_for(bus: Bus, cable: str) -> Route | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The route on ``bus`` that works with ``cable``, or None.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    for route in bus.routes:\\n        if route.cable == cable:\\n            return route\\n    return None\\n\\n\\ndef routes_for(bus: Bus, cable: str) -> list[Route]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every route on ``bus`` that works with ``cable``, in preference order.\\n\\n    A bus can be reachable under more than one adapter protocol. ``route_for``\\n    returns the preferred one and is what normal operations use; this returns\\n    the full candidate list, so a passive listen can try them all before\\n    concluding a bus is silent.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return [route for route in bus.routes if route.cable == cable]\\n\\n\\ndef buses_for_cable(cable: str) -> list[Bus]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Buses reachable with ``cable``, in preference order.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    result = []\\n    for bus in BUSES.values():\\n        if route_for(bus, cable) is not None:\\n            result.append(bus)\\n    return result\\n\\n\\ndef header_bits_for_protocol(stn_protocol: str) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"11 or 29, per the STN STP preset (or ELM short form).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    return _HEADER_BITS_BY_PROTOCOL[stn_protocol]\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"serverClassifierContext\":{\"request\":\"8bfc4697-ca2c-4bae-bf73-5eb398bede25\",\"context\":{\"git_state\":{\"cwd\":\"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers\",\"root\":null,\"branch\":null,\"default_branch\":null,\"status\":null,\"visibility\":null,\"error\":\"pending\"},\"live_cwd\":\"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers\",\"platform\":\"windows\"}},\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"3527319a-abde-42c2-b4f5-2345fabe80f4\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\mcp-servers\",\"sessionId\":\"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\",\"version\":\"2.1.282\",\"gitBranch\":\"HEAD\",\"slug\":\"binary-splashing-comet\"}\ndocs/sessions/raw/2026-10-13/7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17/tasks/a064032b3180b0755.output:72:{\"parentUuid\":\"51c17efd-b29f-4ce8-af42-7b572842f367\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"18814b70-8b7e-4c43-946c-5c9dac496990\",\"agentId\":\"a064032b3180b0755\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01G5YmtsLYdCsKQxyRn6APzL\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"This matches the dossier's own computed states (`cuore/live/ops.py`,\\n`systems_map_bridge.py`): clearing a code is never the same as fixing it;\\nonly a from-car readiness read with the relevant monitor complete can move\\na system from `CLEARED_UNVERIFIED` to `VERIFIED_CLEAN`.\\n\\n## 4. Test A procedure reference\\n\\nPrimary procedure: `docs/vehicles/ZASFAKPN5J7B88115/pdf/Stelvio wiTECH Test\\nA - ESIM Switch.pdf` (full version) or `...Test A - ESIM Switch (1\\npage).pdf` (quick-reference). If Test A fails, follow with the wiring test:\\n`docs/vehicles/ZASFAKPN5J7B88115/pdf/Stelvio ESIM Wiring Test (1\\npage).pdf`. Background and the full diagnostic story (why Test A is the\\nnext step after three clean smoke tests and all-new EVAP parts) is in\\n`docs/vehicles/ZASFAKPN5J7B88115/CASE.md`.\\n\\n## 5. Safety\\n\\n- **No clears before Test A runs and is recorded.** `clear_module_dtcs()`\\n  and `clear_dtcs()` are DESTRUCTIVE TO EVIDENCE -- they erase the exact\\n  codes, snapshots and counters that prove whether a repair worked. Test A\\n  must be run and its result recorded on the Tests surface first. Clearing\\n  afterward is fine and expected (it starts the \\\"unverified repair\\\" clock\\n  that the next readiness read closes).\\n- **Exact consent phrases are required for anything that writes to the\\n  car**, and none of them are offered by this runbook's steps 1-15 above\\n  (which are all reads): `CLEAR <MODULE>` (e.g. `CLEAR ECM`) for\\n  `clear_module_dtcs`; `ACTUATE <MODULE> <NAME>` (e.g. `ACTUATE ECM\\n  EVAPORATION CONTROL VALVE`) or `RUN ROUTINE <MODULE> <NAME>` for\\n  `run_actuator`. Typos or paraphrases are refused, not auto-corrected.\\n- **Blocked modules** -- `run_actuator` and similar writes refuse outright\\n  on safety-critical modules: ABS, EPS, ORC, HALF, DASM, ESL, TVM, TCM,\\n  ESM, DTCM, RFHUB, and anything on the CAN-CH bus. Use MultiEcuScan or\\n  wiTECH for those, never a replay through obd2-mcp.\\n- **No HTTP route ever writes to the car.** Clears, actuator tests and\\n  routines are MCP-tool-only by design (no corresponding `POST` write\\n  route in cuore's API) so that a browser tab or a stray HTTP client can\\n  never trigger one by accident.\\n- `run_actuator` additionally refuses unless the vehicle reads engine-off\\n  and stationary, and always attempts to hand control back to the ECU\\n  afterward even if a step fails -- read `outcome`, `control_returned`\\n  and `session_restored` in its result; if either flag is false, switch\\n  the ignition off immediately.\\n\\n## 6. Troubleshooting\\n\\n| Symptom | Likely cause | What to do |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `list_ports()` does not list COM3 at all | Adapter not plugged in, wrong cable, or Windows assigned a different COM number this time | Check Device Manager for the actual port; re-run `list_ports()`; use the port it actually shows, not a remembered one. |\\n| `connect()` succeeds but every read times out / \\\"NO DATA\\\" | Bus silent -- wrong bus selected, ignition off, or a dead cable segment | Confirm ignition is on (engine need not be running for most reads); check `buses()` and `verify_bus(bus=\\\"can_c\\\")` for passive traffic; try `set_cable()` if the wrong cable profile is declared. |\\n| `connect()` / any read raises `Refused`/`LinkUnavailable` mentioning MultiEcuScan | MES is holding the port -- `mes_state()` shows `state: \\\"connected\\\"` | Close MES or disconnect its session; re-check `mes_state()` until it reads `not_running` or `disconnected`, then retry. |\\n| Any per-call read (`read_pid`, `scan_modules`, etc.) raises `Refused: a live-data poll session is running and holds the adapter` | The poller (step 8) is still running and holds the one adapter session; this is the poller refusing a write/read while it holds the port, exactly as designed | Call `live_session_stop()` first, then retry the read; or use `live_snapshot()` instead of a per-call read while the session is active. |\\n| `connect()` fails citing a stale adapter lock | A previous cuore/obd2-mcp process crashed without releasing `cuore/live/interlock.py`'s lock file | `status()` or `audit_log()` to confirm the lock's PID is dead; the lock is advisory and self-heals once the dead PID is detected, but if it does not, the lock file path is reported in the error -- remove it only after confirming the PID is not a live process. |\\n| Readiness read looks fine but the Systems page still shows `CLEARED_UNVERIFIED`, not `VERIFIED_CLEAN` | The read was not actually from the car (demo/replay/simulated stream), or the monitor the system needs is not among the ones reported complete | Re-run `read_readiness()` live, with the adapter connected to the real car, and confirm the result's `at` timestamp is recent and the source stream starts with `serial`. |\\n| Live board / gauges page shows values but they never change | Session may be using a replay recording instead of the live poller, or the channel's rate is slower than you are watching | Confirm which session is active via `status()`/`live_snapshot()` HTTP equivalents; check the channel's configured rate in `live_channels()`. |\\n\\n## 7. Bus capture, learn-a-signal and per-bus presets (blue A5 / grey A6)\\n\\nThe garage has two bypass cables: the **blue A5** re-pins the adapter onto\\nCAN-IHS (pins 3/11 -- body/comfort/infotainment); the **grey A6** re-pins\\nit onto CAN-CH (pins 12/13 -- chassis/ADAS: ABS, EPS, ORC...). Everything\\nbelow is read-only (passive listen, `STCMM 0` +","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"C:\\Users\\User\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\tool-results\\btg4h2yf8.txt","persistedOutputSize":318084},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7b9952b6-1c05-4cef-b08f-b2815b79e611","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"github","host":"github.com","remote":"dangelojohn/CUORE","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0114a9a5-a0db-4afb-876d-f96a2ff44133","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
