{"parentUuid":"8294a74b-02e6-4f78-98d2-d0d6db8d34a6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac3048c66f3643aa6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2akoTdJLEYETuskMAXA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":268901,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":420,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"79198346-f4d7-4229-b31d-033b70f89bfb","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cg2ako8YR54vh5sjmHT9z","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a41bb871-9d8e-445f-8ff1-518dc57a80d8","timestamp":"2026-10-14T18:13:10.920Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"a41bb871-9d8e-445f-8ff1-518dc57a80d8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac3048c66f3643aa6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2akoTdJLEYETuskMAXA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018WyJhykGf4C5irJMWVsLFi","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\07-first-live-session.md","offset":316,"limit":52},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":268901,"output_tokens":251,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":128},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":420},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":251,"cache_read_input_tokens":268901,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":420,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018WyJhykGf4C5irJMWVsLFi":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\07-first-live-session.md","offset":316,"limit":52}},"serverClassifierRequest":"79198346-f4d7-4229-b31d-033b70f89bfb","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg2ako8YR54vh5sjmHT9z","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b63fbf6b-360f-4162-90e5-545d45ca87c0","timestamp":"2026-10-14T18:13:11.852Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"b63fbf6b-360f-4162-90e5-545d45ca87c0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"3b2e7c35-1a45-4dd2-a323-bff2a4559d42","agentId":"ac3048c66f3643aa6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WyJhykGf4C5irJMWVsLFi","type":"tool_result","content":"316\t## 7. Bus capture, learn-a-signal and per-bus presets (blue A5 / grey A6)\n317\t\n318\tThe garage has two bypass cables: the **blue A5** re-pins the adapter onto\n319\tCAN-IHS (pins 3/11 -- body/comfort/infotainment); the **grey A6** re-pins\n320\tit onto CAN-CH (pins 12/13 -- chassis/ADAS: ABS, EPS, ORC...). Everything\n321\tbelow is read-only (passive listen, `STCMM 0` + `STM`/`ATMA`) -- the\n322\texisting write guards for ABS/EPS/ORC and anything on CAN-CH are untouched\n323\tand still refuse without explicit confirmation.\n324\t\n325\t**Declare the cable first.** Fit the cable, then `set_cable(\"blue_a5\")` or\n326\t`set_cable(\"grey_a6\")` (MCP tool, or the Live board's \"Change cable\"\n327\tcontrol at `/v/{vin}/liveboard`, which also lists what the new declaration\n328\tenables before you confirm). Every bus-capture and learn call below\n329\trefuses with `Refused` if the bus it targets is not reachable with the\n330\tcurrently declared cable, or if the poller/MultiEcuScan holds the adapter.\n331\t\n332\t**Bus capture** -- the Live board's \"Bus capture\" panel (same Start/Stop/\n333\tSave shape as the Freeze frame panel above it): pick the bus the fitted\n334\tcable reaches, Start, watch the live frame rate and distinct-ID count,\n335\tStop, then Save. Save writes a CSV recording in the same wire format\n336\tcuore's own live sessions use, named `buscapture_<bus>_<cable>_<time>.csv`\n337\tunder the recordings directory, and logs a from-car observation (kind\n338\t`\"bus_capture\"`) carrying the recording path and id counts. The MCP tools\n339\tare `bus_capture_start(bus)`, `bus_capture_stop(bus)`,\n340\t`bus_capture_save(bus, vin=...)`.\n341\t\n342\t**Learn a signal** -- `/v/{vin}/learn`: pick the bus, name the physical\n343\taction you're about to do (the page suggests a few per bus -- \"press the\n344\tbrake pedal\", \"turn the wheel\", \"open the driver door\", \"switch the HVAC\n345\tfan\"), Start, hold the action for a few seconds, Stop. The page ranks\n346\tevery `(CAN id, byte offset)` by how much it changed during that window\n347\tand lets you name the best candidate and save it. A saved signal is\n348\tlogged with `scale: \"unknown\"` -- nothing here ever guesses a physical\n349\tunit from one capture -- and shows on the Live board as a raw channel\n350\tlabelled \"learned, unscaled\". The MCP tools are `learn_start(bus,\n351\taction)` and `learn_stop(bus)`; naming and saving the chosen candidate is\n352\ta page action (`POST /api/buscapture/{bus}/learn/accept`), not an MCP\n353\ttool.\n354\t\n355\t**Per-bus presets** -- `chassis_a6` (CAN-CH: ABS wheel speeds, steering\n356\tangle, yaw rate) and `body_a5` (CAN-IHS: HVAC temperature, battery\n357\tmonitor, door states) list only what a public broadcast-signal source\n358\t(`cuore.live.did_catalog.BROADCAST_SIGNALS`) or this VIN's own learned\n359\tsignals actually cover; anything else is shown `unknown_did` and is never\n360\tpolled or implied to exist (brake pressure, for example, has no known\n361\tbroadcast signal or DID on this platform and always shows `unknown_did`\n362\tin `chassis_a6`). The Live board shows each preset's required cable and\n363\trefuses to start it (`Refused`) without that cable declared.\n364\t\n365\t<!-- cable-reference:start (generated by docs/handbook/generate_cable_reference.py -- do not hand-edit between these markers; re-run the script instead) -->\n366\t\n367\t## 8. Which cable for which module"}]},"uuid":"a187f6bb-fbf1-473a-a7c2-251c30c9a4d3","timestamp":"2026-10-14T18:13:11.878Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\07-first-live-session.md","content":"## 7. Bus capture, learn-a-signal and per-bus presets (blue A5 / grey A6)\n\nThe garage has two bypass cables: the **blue A5** re-pins the adapter onto\nCAN-IHS (pins 3/11 -- body/comfort/infotainment); the **grey A6** re-pins\nit onto CAN-CH (pins 12/13 -- chassis/ADAS: ABS, EPS, ORC...). Everything\nbelow is read-only (passive listen, `STCMM 0` + `STM`/`ATMA`) -- the\nexisting write guards for ABS/EPS/ORC and anything on CAN-CH are untouched\nand still refuse without explicit confirmation.\n\n**Declare the cable first.** Fit the cable, then `set_cable(\"blue_a5\")` or\n`set_cable(\"grey_a6\")` (MCP tool, or the Live board's \"Change cable\"\ncontrol at `/v/{vin}/liveboard`, which also lists what the new declaration\nenables before you confirm). Every bus-capture and learn call below\nrefuses with `Refused` if the bus it targets is not reachable with the\ncurrently declared cable, or if the poller/MultiEcuScan holds the adapter.\n\n**Bus capture** -- the Live board's \"Bus capture\" panel (same Start/Stop/\nSave shape as the Freeze frame panel above it): pick the bus the fitted\ncable reaches, Start, watch the live frame rate and distinct-ID count,\nStop, then Save. Save writes a CSV recording in the same wire format\ncuore's own live sessions use, named `buscapture_<bus>_<cable>_<time>.csv`\nunder the recordings directory, and logs a from-car observation (kind\n`\"bus_capture\"`) carrying the recording path and id counts. The MCP tools\nare `bus_capture_start(bus)`, `bus_capture_stop(bus)`,\n`bus_capture_save(bus, vin=...)`.\n\n**Learn a signal** -- `/v/{vin}/learn`: pick the bus, name the physical\naction you're about to do (the page suggests a few per bus -- \"press the\nbrake pedal\", \"turn the wheel\", \"open the driver door\", \"switch the HVAC\nfan\"), Start, hold the action for a few seconds, Stop. The page ranks\nevery `(CAN id, byte offset)` by how much it changed during that window\nand lets you name the best candidate and save it. A saved signal is\nlogged with `scale: \"unknown\"` -- nothing here ever guesses a physical\nunit from one capture -- and shows on the Live board as a raw channel\nlabelled \"learned, unscaled\". The MCP tools are `learn_start(bus,\naction)` and `learn_stop(bus)`; naming and saving the chosen candidate is\na page action (`POST /api/buscapture/{bus}/learn/accept`), not an MCP\ntool.\n\n**Per-bus presets** -- `chassis_a6` (CAN-CH: ABS wheel speeds, steering\nangle, yaw rate) and `body_a5` (CAN-IHS: HVAC temperature, battery\nmonitor, door states) list only what a public broadcast-signal source\n(`cuore.live.did_catalog.BROADCAST_SIGNALS`) or this VIN's own learned\nsignals actually cover; anything else is shown `unknown_did` and is never\npolled or implied to exist (brake pressure, for example, has no known\nbroadcast signal or DID on this platform and always shows `unknown_did`\nin `chassis_a6`). The Live board shows each preset's required cable and\nrefuses to start it (`Refused`) without that cable declared.\n\n<!-- cable-reference:start (generated by docs/handbook/generate_cable_reference.py -- do not hand-edit between these markers; re-run the script instead) -->\n\n## 8. Which cable for which module","numLines":52,"startLine":316,"totalLines":412}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b63fbf6b-360f-4162-90e5-545d45ca87c0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
