{"parentUuid":"bd22a3f6-bb6f-4148-bbe5-85216f0571f4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b04a6688-8f21-49a8-8854-1f6c72f12ba2","agentId":"ac3048c66f3643aa6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nr18cojffZGhAGpuytmKj5","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Guards ``docs/mobile/API_CONTRACT.md`` against drift.\n\nThat document is the contract a native iPhone app (Swift or Flutter) talks\nto in place of the phone web page ``/m/{vin}``. It was generated by reading\n``app.openapi()`` once; this check re-reads ``app.openapi()`` on every run\nand fails if any ``(method, path)`` row in the doc's own \"Path table\" is no\nlonger present in the live schema -- the one way a doc like this silently\ngoes stale is someone renaming or removing a route without knowing a mobile\nclient depends on it.\n\nThis does not attempt to fail on *additions* (a new route showing up in the\nschema that the doc does not yet mention) -- only disappearance of a\ndocumented one, which is the breaking case for a client already built\nagainst this contract.\n\nSame posture as every other ``check_*.py`` here: plain script, ``check()``,\nexit 1 on failure, no pytest. ``CUORE_STATE_DIR`` is pointed at a throwaway\ndirectory before ``cuore`` is imported, so this needs no real corpus.\n\nRun:\n    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_api_contract.py\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"78204a16-886d-4d0c-9f02-b876e64e6228","timestamp":"2026-10-14T18:18:27.703Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Guards ``docs/mobile/API_CONTRACT.md`` against drift.\n\nThat document is the contract a native iPhone app (Swift or Flutter) talks\nto in place of the phone web page ``/m/{vin}``. It was generated by reading\n``app.openapi()`` once; this check re-reads ``app.openapi()`` on every run\nand fails if any ``(method, path)`` row in the doc's own \"Path table\" is no\nlonger present in the live schema -- the one way a doc like this silently\ngoes stale is someone renaming or removing a route without knowing a mobile\nclient depends on it.\n\nThis does not attempt to fail on *additions* (a new route showing up in the\nschema that the doc does not yet mention) -- only disappearance of a\ndocumented one, which is the breaking case for a client already built\nagainst this contract.\n\nSame posture as every other ``check_*.py`` here: plain script, ``check()``,\nexit 1 on failure, no pytest. ``CUORE_STATE_DIR`` is pointed at a throwaway\ndirectory before ``cuore`` is imported, so this needs no real corpus.\n\nRun:\n    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_api_contract.py\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"352b3209-3e79-4441-8d47-f11814ad677d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":6},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"github","host":"github.com","remote":"dangelojohn/CUORE","visibility":"unknown"}],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bd22a3f6-bb6f-4148-bbe5-85216f0571f4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
