{"parentUuid":"037191f3-4607-4c1c-8d53-5921630266c2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac3048c66f3643aa6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2bFdas9R7kV5bdXBLf5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pushed to `github main` at commit `a6b11ab`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":204,"cache_read_input_tokens":309312,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":204,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c56f424a-284e-4474-baa6-7d1142ae471e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cg2bFdEXuB5dWKpqQRr8x","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1a5291dd-e2c7-4495-9c7d-d2701c99cb95","timestamp":"2026-10-14T18:19:40.851Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"1a5291dd-e2c7-4495-9c7d-d2701c99cb95","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac3048c66f3643aa6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2bFdas9R7kV5bdXBLf5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QS74CeHhgKtFWqZByyhKJB","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Built and shipped the MES-learn feature. Commit a6b11ab, pushed to github/main (never touched forge or koch-mcp/).\n\nFiles (all new unless noted):\n- cuore/live/mes_learn.py — two-adapter guard (_check_two_adapters: refuses empty port, <2 serial ports, or port == MES's own Interface-0 port); start/stop/status/candidates/accept/reject lifecycle (mirrors buscapture.py's thread model, passive=True + allow_while_mes_connected=True, never transmits); align(frames, recording) — pure function: learn.uds_transactions -> learn.did_series -> per-CSV-column OLS fit over every (target,DID,offset,width,signed) combo, confident only at R²>=0.98 and >=20 distinct raw values, else \"no confident match\".\n- cuore/live/learned.py (additive) — CONFIDENCE_MES=\"SINGLE-SOURCE (learned)\", accept_mes/reject_mes/learned_mes, and learned_mes_channels(vin) which hands back ready Channel objects (same hand-off posture as ui_store.load_custom_channels) with a CarScanner-style formula. Formula builder sign-corrects the high byte alone, (SIGNED(hi)*256)+lo, not SIGNED((hi*256)+lo) — readall._signed() guesses width by magnitude and misreads a 16-bit value with a zero high byte as 8-bit; this is the correct, unambiguous equivalent (found and fixed via a failing test).\n- cuore/api/mes_learn.py + cuore/web/mes_learn_routes.py + templates/mes_learn.html — POST/GET /api/mes-learn/{start,stop,status,candidates,candidates/{id}/accept|reject}; GET /v/{vin}/learn-mes review page.\n- obd2-mcp/server.py — new marked ADDITIVE block: mes_learn_start/stop/status/candidates/accept MCP tools, via _via() same as buscapture's.\n- cuore/app.py — include_router pairs for the new API and web routers.\n- docs/handbook/07-first-live-session.md — new \"## 9. Learning module parameters from MES\" section (hardware list, procedure, MCP tools).\n- cuore/tests/check_mes_learn.py — 56 checks, all green: guard refusals; align() on a synthetic two-module/three-DID capture (ECM 2-byte signed temp scale 0.1 offset -40, ECM 1-byte decoy, TCM 1-byte gear) + synthetic MES CSV — temp fit correctly (module/DID/field/scale/offset/R²), gear correctly \"no confident match\" (only 9 distinct raw values < 20), decoy never wins; full start->stop->candidates->accept/reject lifecycle over a FakeBus (asserts every sent command is AT/ST-prefixed, i.e. never transmits); accept -> learned_mes_channels -> formula reproduces original values via readall.eval_formula; HTTP/page smoke checks.\n\nAlso ran check_learn.py (61), check_buscapture.py (44), check_api_contract.py (87) and an obd2-mcp/server.py import smoke test — all pass, nothing else regressed. No real COM port ever opened; no subagents used."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":204,"cache_read_input_tokens":309312,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":204,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QS74CeHhgKtFWqZByyhKJB":{"message":"Built and shipped the MES-learn feature. Commit a6b11ab, pushed to github/main (never touched forge or koch-mcp/).\n\nFiles (all new unless noted):\n- cuore/live/mes_learn.py — two-adapter guard (_check_two_adapters: refuses empty port, <2 serial ports, or port == MES's own Interface-0 port); start/stop/status/candidates/accept/reject lifecycle (mirrors buscapture.py's thread model, passive=True + allow_while_mes_connected=True, never transmits); align(frames, recording) — pure function: learn.uds_transactions -> learn.did_series -> per-CSV-column OLS fit over every (target,DID,offset,width,signed) combo, confident only at R²>=0.98 and >=20 distinct raw values, else \"no confident match\".\n- cuore/live/learned.py (additive) — CONFIDENCE_MES=\"SINGLE-SOURCE (learned)\", accept_mes/reject_mes/learned_mes, and learned_mes_channels(vin) which hands back ready Channel objects (same hand-off posture as ui_store.load_custom_channels) with a CarScanner-style formula. Formula builder sign-corrects the high byte alone, (SIGNED(hi)*256)+lo, not SIGNED((hi*256)+lo) — readall._signed() guesses width by magnitude and misreads a 16-bit value with a zero high byte as 8-bit; this is the correct, unambiguous equivalent (found and fixed via a failing test).\n- cuore/api/mes_learn.py + cuore/web/mes_learn_routes.py + templates/mes_learn.html — POST/GET /api/mes-learn/{start,stop,status,candidates,candidates/{id}/accept|reject}; GET /v/{vin}/learn-mes review page.\n- obd2-mcp/server.py — new marked ADDITIVE block: mes_learn_start/stop/status/candidates/accept MCP tools, via _via() same as buscapture's.\n- cuore/app.py — include_router pairs for the new API and web routers.\n- docs/handbook/07-first-live-session.md — new \"## 9. Learning module parameters from MES\" section (hardware list, procedure, MCP tools).\n- cuore/tests/check_mes_learn.py — 56 checks, all green: guard refusals; align() on a synthetic two-module/three-DID capture (ECM 2-byte signed temp scale 0.1 offset -40, ECM 1-byte decoy, TCM 1-byte gear) + synthetic MES CSV — temp fit correctly (module/DID/field/scale/offset/R²), gear correctly \"no confident match\" (only 9 distinct raw values < 20), decoy never wins; full start->stop->candidates->accept/reject lifecycle over a FakeBus (asserts every sent command is AT/ST-prefixed, i.e. never transmits); accept -> learned_mes_channels -> formula reproduces original values via readall.eval_formula; HTTP/page smoke checks.\n\nAlso ran check_learn.py (61), check_buscapture.py (44), check_api_contract.py (87) and an obd2-mcp/server.py import smoke test — all pass, nothing else regressed. No real COM port ever opened; no subagents used."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c56f424a-284e-4474-baa6-7d1142ae471e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg2bFdEXuB5dWKpqQRr8x","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"af292e66-bc52-4b30-bd63-f9e35dfc5656","timestamp":"2026-10-14T18:19:53.801Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
